SUBENT        D0007001   20171122   20171122   20171122       D112D0007  1    1 
BIB                 16         53                                 D0007  1    2 
TITLE      Unified absolute differential cross sections for       D0007  1    3 
            neutron production by the hydrogen isotopes for       D0007  1    4 
            charged-particle energies between 6 and 17 MeV        D0007  1    5 
AUTHOR     (M.Drosg)                                              D0007  1    6 
INSTITUTE  (1USALAS,2AUSVIE)                                      D0007  1    7 
REFERENCE  (J,NSE,67,190,1978)                                    D0007  1    8 
           (R,LA-6262-MS,1976) Prelim. Ed=7 and 10MeV data        D0007  1    9 
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USALAS)                                         D0007  1   10 
            with a time of flight system. Klystron buncher used.  D0007  1   11 
INC-SPECT  The entrance foil was made of molybdenum and the beam  D0007  1   12 
           stop was made of gold. the absolute value of the energyD0007  1   13 
           loss is known to about +-0.02MeV. The energy spread is D0007  1   14 
           less than 0.1MeV(fwhm).                                D0007  1   15 
SAMPLE     The target (sample) cell, about 3 cm long, was filled  D0007  1   16 
           with tritium at a pressure of ca. 1.7 atm.  The cell   D0007  1   17 
           was cooled by a fine jet of air                        D0007  1   18 
METHOD     (TOF) flight path = 256 cm. quasi-absolute method.     D0007  1   19 
           The relative efficiency of the long liquid scinti-     D0007  1   20 
           llator was determined originally by H-1(n,n)H-1,  and  D0007  1   21 
           it was checked over a wide range by means of           D0007  1   22 
           H-3(d,n)He-4 and H-2(d,n)He-4 reactions.               D0007  1   23 
           To establish an absolute scale for the tof measurementsD0007  1   24 
           the same cross-section standard and the same experimentD0007  1   25 
           conditions were used for all 3 reactions, H-3(p,n)He-3,D0007  1   26 
           H-3(d,n)He-4 and h-2(d,n)he-3 (and also for H2(t,n)He4)D0007  1   27 
           The experimental setup has been calibrated with        D0007  1   28 
           appropriate reference cross section, rather than       D0007  1   29 
           normalizing relative angular distribution to an        D0007  1   30 
           absolute 0-deg excitation.                             D0007  1   31 
DETECTOR   (SCIN)                                                 D0007  1   32 
           12 cm diameter by 6-cm long liquid scintillator, NE-213D0007  1   33 
            coupled to a 56 avp photo-tube.                       D0007  1   34 
REL-REF    (M,,M.Drosg,J,NIM,105,573,1972)                        D0007  1   35 
            Counting efficiency determination                     D0007  1   36 
PART-DET   (N)                                                    D0007  1   37 
MONITOR    Absolute, tof method with a well established efficiencyD0007  1   38 
           curve by H-1(n,el)H-1 scattering experiment.           D0007  1   39 
CORRECTION To obtain the data with accuracy as close to 1 percent D0007  1   40 
           as possible, whenever an effect was found to be larger D0007  1   41 
           than 0.5 percent, the data were corrected              D0007  1   42 
           correspondingly.                                       D0007  1   43 
ERR-ANALYS The combination of the statistical uncertainty with theD0007  1   44 
           uncertainty of the background subtraction.             D0007  1   45 
STATUS     (APRVD) approved by M.Drosg,79/03/06.comment+correct'n D0007  1   46 
